ALGORITHMS RE-IMPLEMENTED

tiny-skia — https://github.com/linebender/tiny-skia
  BSD-3-Clause. Copyright (c) 2011 Google Inc.; Copyright (c) 2020 Yevhenii
  Reizner. tiny-skia is a port of Skia and its licence carries both notices.
  The anti-aliased scan converter, hairline stroking, cubic and quadratic
  subdivision counts, dash-splitting rules, lowp blend arithmetic, f32
  layer-compositing pipeline and gradient evaluation in
  LeanSvg/{Raster,Geom,Canvas,Shader}.lean are fixed-point Lean
  re-implementations of its algorithms. No Rust or C++ source is included.

BEHAVIOURAL REFERENCES

resvg and usvg — https://github.com/linebender/resvg
  Apache-2.0 OR MIT, as declared in the workspace manifest at tag v0.48.1 and
  on main. Releases prior to the relicensing were MPL-2.0. Used as the
  rendering oracle and as the reference for SVG semantics. No source included.

simplecss — https://github.com/linebender/simplecss
  Apache-2.0 OR MIT. The CSS selector subset in LeanSvg/Css.lean follows its
  grammar.

svgtypes — https://github.com/linebender/svgtypes
  Apache-2.0 OR MIT. Colour, length and transform parsing follow its
  behaviour.

